// Type-checking config — the build (tsup + tsconfig.json) emits from `src` only, so `src` is all it
// needs to compile. But the tests are where the *public* types actually get used, and they run under
// tsx, which strips types without checking them: a method missing from an interface it is meant to
// describe is invisible to both. That is exactly how `BoundedField` came to omit `sampleGrad`,
// `qCriterion`, `lambda2` and `stretching` while `BoundedFieldImpl` implemented all four — callable
// at runtime, rejected by `tsc`. Checking `test` too closes that gap.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"]
}
